{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The screw hooks and screw-mounted magnets fit my repeated interest in fastening and mounting; I can see them working with my screws, rivet nuts, and bolts to secure things or make removable fixtures.",
    "The pegboard and duct tape support the same hands-on work: keeping tools accessible and making temporary repairs alongside my existing adhesive supplies."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The water tester and CO2 monitor are measuring devices, but they answer questions I have no current reason to investigate. My caliper and infrared thermometer purchases do not mean I need every kind of meter.",
    "The bottle brush connects to a bottle purchase from years ago rather than my recent projects, while the delivery backpack, anatomy models, and retail display serve activities my history does not suggest I am doing."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Having a practical or technical use seems to have counted too heavily, even when the item would not help with my repair and fabrication work.",
    "Broad connections such as measuring, storage, or bottles seem to have outweighed the specific purpose and timing of my purchases."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated recent purchases of rivets, threaded inserts, bolts, drilling supplies, and a grommet press point toward joining materials and installing hardware.",
    "Useful next choices should complement equipment and supplies I already have; a new specialized instrument needs a relevant project, not just a resemblance to another tool I bought."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You partly recognized my workshop needs, but stretched that interest into unrelated equipment without a clear connection to my current projects."
}"}
